---
Golden coverage for P7.2 (#1300)'s `brand_assertion` fix: a `uses`-commons
named type reaching the entry as an HTTP POST body and as a queue message.
`deserialise_Cents` is a straight re-export from `money.js` and so returns the
*unbranded* commons `Cents`, while `intake.call`/`credit.message` (in
`handlers.ts`) are typed against the *branded* `Cents` this context rebrands —
without the entry-side brand-assertion cast, `tsc --strict` rejects both
generated projects.
---
context api

uses money

service intake from http {
  on POST("/cents") (body: Cents) -> Effect[HttpResult[Int]] by v: Visitor {
    Created(body)
  }
}

service credit from queue("cents-credited") {
  on message(amount: Cents) -> Effect[QueueResult] {
    Ack
  }
}
